  "title": "A doubled edge hides the sign of a parallel path from acyclic counts",
  "subject": "Equal acyclic counts of non-isomorphic signed graphs in the genus-2 twist map",
  "conclusion": "Flipping the sign of a path through degree-2 vertices whose ends are also joined by links of both signs keeps a signed graph's chromatic polynomial, and so its number of acyclic orientations, though not its Tutte polynomial. One such flip explains each of the 48 skeletons that isomorphic pieces left unexplained on L(3,1,3,1), so every exact twist relation found on the genus-2 surfaces now holds skeleton by skeleton.",
